# Agent Workflow

Use the same operating flow in every project.

## Canonical Flow

```text
intake -> source-of-truth read -> plan/checkpoint -> /goal -> subagent findings -> main patch -> verification -> evidence -> memory -> lesson promotion
```

## Hard Rules

- One main agent owns final edits.
- Subagents are read-only unless a checkpoint explicitly assigns a narrow disjoint write scope.
- Non-trivial work needs a plan or checkpoint spec before implementation.
- Every checkpoint needs scope, anti-scope, verification, evidence path and stop condition.
- Verification must match the risk and blast radius.
- State must live in files, not only in chat.
- Research links become research notes first, then patterns, then playbook/rule changes if reusable.

## Stop Instead Of Guessing

Stop and record a blocker when required credentials, payment/provider approval, deploy access, official-doc verification, or local test ability is missing.

Do not invent proof. A narrow check cannot prove a broad requirement.
